  "lineage": "Opera of northeastern Guangxi centred on Guilin, sung in Guilin dialect, a Southwestern Mandarin; its main music is tanqiang (nanlu and beilu, kin to erhuang and xipi), with some gaoqiang and kunqiang. It entered China's national intangible heritage list in 2006. A huqin fiddle leads (the erhu card stands in), with moon lute and sanxian, over drum and gong.",
